gclib skips, without a word, features it cannot place in a transcript, lines
with too few columns and coordinates it cannot read. This entry point,
linked in front of gffcompare's and trmap's mains, reads every annotation
and sequence file first and refuses those; for gffcompare, --bc-* options
name the files its outputs are moved to. The Makefile links it into both
programs.

gffcompare's main ends without a return, which only main may do: it now
returns 0.

